# Build output and throwaway run artifacts.
/dist
/out-tsc
/tmp
/artifacts
/coverage

# Markdown is hand-wrapped prose with a lot of tables. Prettier pads every table
# cell to the widest entry and rewrites *emphasis* as _emphasis_, so a one-line
# edit to a doc lands as a few hundred lines of realignment and buries itself.
*.md

# Machine-generated reference tables. These are regenerated wholesale from the
# MATLAB verification runs, so reformatting them is noise that would also make
# the next regeneration look like a change.
/src/test-data/verification

# Storybook docs pages. Prettier's MDX printer rewrites the `*` of a JSX comment
# (`{/* … */}`) as `_`, which breaks the comment.
*.mdx

# A rendering of a brief, kept beside its PDF. Not source.
/docs/*.html

# The numerical oracle's problem and reference files, written by its Python
# generator (oracle/pmks_oracle/run.py, benchmarks/derivations/). Like the
# MATLAB tables above, they are regenerated wholesale and must not be reflowed.
/oracle/benchmarks/cases
/src/test-data/oracle

# The oracle's Python environment (uv sync); oracle/.gitignore keeps it out of git.
/oracle/.venv
